 "title": "Vascular disease after the first event decision chart: after a myocardial infarction, cardiac rehabilitation and the drugs that prevent the next event (ACE inhibitor and statin for all, beta blocker only with a low ejection fraction); in the leg, acute limb ischemia is embolic or thrombotic and is anticoagulated and revascularized within hours, while chronic disease is claudication treated with ABCDES or critical limb ischemia that needs revascularization",
